        "question_text": "<p>Which heat treatment process is used to <i>increase the hardness</i> of steel by heating it to a high temperature and then rapidly cooling it in water or oil?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Quenching is the heat treatment process where steel is heated to a high temperature (austenitizing temperature) and then rapidly cooled in water, oil, or other quenching media to increase its hardness. Annealing, tempering, and normalizing are other heat treatment processes with different purposes.</p>",
